{{- /*
fingerprint.tmpl — comment-only dependency fingerprint block for run_onchange_
scripts (the canonical form of the script-prefix policy in AGENTS.md).

Emits one `#   <path>  <sha256>` line per file matched by each glob pattern, and
one `#   value:<name>  <sha256>` line per declared value.
chezmoi hashes the whole rendered script to decide whether to re-run it, so a
changed dependency changes the rendered content and re-triggers the script.

`include . | sha256sum` hashes file CONTENT (a bare `sha256sum .` would hash
the path STRING); the `(stat .).isDir` guard skips the directories a `**`
glob matches. For a `.tmpl` dependency this hashes the raw template text
(its onepasswordRead refs, not resolved secrets), so no secret ever enters
the fingerprint.

`values` exists for ONE purpose: a `transient-blocking` skip site (see
skip.sh.tmpl) exits 0 and is recorded as a successful run, so it can only
re-run on its own if the rendered content changes when its precondition
appears. Hashing a capabilities.tmpl probe token here is what supplies that
change. A value must be a two-valued token from capabilities.tmpl — hashing
anything that varies per render (a timestamp, a counter) turns every consumer
into an always-run script. An empty value fails the render, for the same
reason a zero-match glob does: a silently absent dependency is the failure
mode this partial exists to prevent.

Both keys are optional, but at least one must be present. Passing only `globs`
renders exactly as it always has.

Usage (from any script template):

  {{ includeTemplate "fingerprint.tmpl" (dict
       "sourceDir" .chezmoi.sourceDir
       "globs" (list "system/linux/etc/**" ".chezmoidata/fonts.yaml")) }}

  {{ includeTemplate "fingerprint.tmpl" (dict
       "sourceDir" .chezmoi.sourceDir
       "globs"  (list ".chezmoidata/gnome.yaml")
       "values" (list (dict "name" "session-bus-present" "value" $probe))) }}
*/ -}}
{{- $sourceDir := .sourceDir -}}
{{- $globs := list -}}{{- if hasKey . "globs" -}}{{- $globs = .globs -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $values := list -}}{{- if hasKey . "values" -}}{{- $values = .values -}}{{- end -}}
{{- if and (eq (len $globs) 0) (eq (len $values) 0) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "fingerprint.tmpl: called with neither \"globs\" nor \"values\" in %s. A fingerprint block that declares no dependency never re-triggers its script." $sourceDir) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- range $pattern := $globs -}}
{{- $count := 0 -}}
{{- range glob (joinPath $sourceDir $pattern) -}}
{{- if not (stat .).isDir }}
#   {{ . | trimPrefix $sourceDir | trimPrefix "/" }}  {{ include . | sha256sum }}
{{- $count = add $count 1 -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if eq $count 0 -}}
{{- fail (printf "fingerprint.tmpl: glob pattern '%s' matched zero files in %s" $pattern $sourceDir) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- range $entry := $values -}}
{{- if not (kindIs "map" $entry) -}}
{{- fail (printf "fingerprint.tmpl: each \"values\" entry must be a dict with \"name\" and \"value\", got a %s (%v)" (kindOf $entry) $entry) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $name := "" -}}{{- if hasKey $entry "name" -}}{{- $name = $entry.name -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $value := "" -}}{{- if hasKey $entry "value" -}}{{- $value = $entry.value -}}{{- end -}}
{{- if eq $name "" -}}
{{- fail (printf "fingerprint.tmpl: a \"values\" entry is missing \"name\" in %s" $sourceDir) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if eq $value "" -}}
{{- fail (printf "fingerprint.tmpl: value %q rendered empty in %s. A capabilities.tmpl probe always emits a token; an empty one means the probe was misnamed or failed." $name $sourceDir) -}}
{{- end }}
#   value:{{ $name }}  {{ $value | sha256sum }}
{{- end }}
